      "text": "[4:56PM] #Apapa_Ajegunle #TrafficUpdate \n\nMotorists can expect a fast-moving commute from both Ojo Road and Otto Wharf to Ajeromi. At Ajeromi Junction, all commercial buses are currently being diverted to Ojora Way to connect to Boundary Bus Stop.\n\nMovement from Baale Street to the Boundary Roundabout is also progressing well. Furthermore, the stretch of Mobil Road, both inward and outward, is experiencing fast-moving vehicle traffic at this time.\n\nFrom High Bridge/Ijora Oloopa Ramp to Total, traffic is flowing quickly on both lanes. However, shortly after Total by the RRS Junction, one lane is occupied by trucks, while the second lane remains clear for cars and other vehicles.\n\nLastly, vehicles exiting Apapa Front Point Road through the Marine Bridge to Iganmu are also encountering fast-moving traffic. No impediments have been recorded as of this hour, and officers are on ground ensuring smooth traffic flow.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
