    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1929955716896567435",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1929955716896567435",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1929955716896567435",
      "text": "[7:30PM] #Idumota #TrafficUpdate \n\nHigh traffic volume on the route from Oyebanji Roundabout to Adeniji Adele Road via Oba's Palace and Police Post, attributed to ongoing construction work in the area.\nBusy traffic conditions on the stretch from Tinubu Square to Nnamdi Azikiwe Street, en route to Tom Jones Intersection, largely due to market activities.\nSlow movement under the Idumota Bridge, particularly on the inward journey from Eyin Eyo to Balogun and Martin Streets, resulting from bus stop activities along the corridor.\nSmooth traffic flow on Ilubinrin connecting Carter Bridge, inward towards Ijora Olopa, as well as Oyingbo, with vehicles moving at a relatively faster pace.\n\nOfficers remain actively engaged in managing the traffic flow to mitigate congestion.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
